1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,052
Your models are stored, but nothing draws
them yet.

2
00:00:03,112 --> 00:00:07,429
That's the job of the theme blocks — and
you add them once, in Shopify's theme

3
00:00:07,489 --> 00:00:08,089
editor.

4
00:00:09,032 --> 00:00:09,817
There are two.

5
00:00:09,877 --> 00:00:14,708
3D Viewer — Product goes on your product
template and picks the model up from the

6
00:00:14,768 --> 00:00:16,037
product automatically.

7
00:00:16,097 --> 00:00:21,109
3D Viewer — Any Model takes a Model ID and
works on any page at all: your home page,

8
00:00:21,169 --> 00:00:22,740
a custom page, a blog post.

9
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:28,220
Start in your Shopify admin under Online
Store, then Themes, then Customize.

10
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:31,669
Make sure the template dropdown at the top
says Product.

11
00:00:32,529 --> 00:00:34,880
In the left sidebar, click Add section.

12
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:38,106
Scroll to the bottom of the list and open
Apps.

13
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:41,748
This is where every app-provided block
lives, not just this one.

14
00:00:42,608 --> 00:00:44,381
Choose 3D Viewer — Product.

15
00:00:45,091 --> 00:00:45,818
And there it is.

16
00:00:45,878 --> 00:00:49,705
The block is in your template and the
viewer is already rendering the model you

17
00:00:49,765 --> 00:00:53,247
assigned to this product — you didn't have
to tell it which file to use.

18
00:00:54,107 --> 00:00:56,032
Its settings are deliberately thin.

19
00:00:56,092 --> 00:01:00,170
Manual model URL is an override for
testing only — leave it blank for the

20
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:00,851
normal flow.

21
00:01:00,911 --> 00:01:05,500
Height and background colour are defaults,
and any per-product setting you save in

22
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:06,804
the app wins over them.

23
00:01:07,664 --> 00:01:12,111
You can drag the block anywhere in the
template — above the product media, below

24
00:01:12,171 --> 00:01:14,702
the description, wherever it fits your
layout.

25
00:01:14,762 --> 00:01:15,491
Then hit Save.

26
00:01:16,351 --> 00:01:20,113
That's the product page done — for every
product in your store at once.

27
00:01:20,173 --> 00:01:24,311
Assign a model to any product and it shows
up here with no further theme work.

28
00:01:25,171 --> 00:01:26,314
Now the other block.

29
00:01:26,374 --> 00:01:31,063
Pick a different template from the same
dropdown — here I've switched to Page —

30
00:01:31,123 --> 00:01:35,091
then Add section, Apps, and this time
choose 3D Viewer — Any Model.

31
00:01:35,951 --> 00:01:39,968
This one needs to be told what to show,
and you have two ways.

32
00:01:40,028 --> 00:01:45,097
Paste a Model ID from the app's 3D Models
library, or paste a direct file URL.

33
00:01:45,157 --> 00:01:47,069
If you fill both, the ID wins.

34
00:01:47,929 --> 00:01:49,172
Always prefer the ID.

35
00:01:49,232 --> 00:01:53,763
It carries the model's saved viewer
settings with it — height, background,

36
00:01:53,823 --> 00:01:55,562
camera, controls, everything.

37
00:01:55,622 --> 00:02:00,588
A raw URL brings only the file, so the
block's own height and background get used

38
00:02:00,648 --> 00:02:01,248
instead.

39
00:02:01,944 --> 00:02:03,903
This block has two extra switches.

40
00:02:03,963 --> 00:02:08,652
Auto rotate spins the model on load, and
Show on-screen controls covers the zoom

41
00:02:08,712 --> 00:02:10,018
and fullscreen buttons.

42
00:02:10,078 --> 00:02:14,827
Note that these only apply when you've
used a raw URL — a Model ID brings its own

43
00:02:14,887 --> 00:02:15,487
settings.

44
00:02:16,222 --> 00:02:20,733
Save, and the model is live on that page —
with its caption underneath if you set

45
00:02:20,793 --> 00:02:21,393
one.

46
00:02:21,819 --> 00:02:25,815
One caveat. App blocks only exist in
Online Store 2. 0 themes.

47
00:02:25,875 --> 00:02:31,180
If Apps isn't in your Add section list,
your template is a legacy liquid one — use

48
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:35,368
the iframe embed code instead, which we
cover in tutorial eight.

49
00:02:36,228 --> 00:02:37,035
Blocks placed.

50
00:02:37,095 --> 00:02:42,240
Next, the part you'll actually repeat for
every product: uploading and assigning the

51
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:43,045
model itself.
